}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"23b0ae3014c0071a818740b3e9b1f1f57dcd04026d1ecc77e753e20c9c8e62b3"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T5c","usage":{"input_tokens":30126,"output_tokens":908,"requests":4}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"f2a74b72945dbc59f128b3f2b217f225d32ba5ac777d954f4e47fdfd5f26f332"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T1","usage":{"input_tokens":62000,"output_tokens":2976,"requests":4}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.75,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile the 'SOLE condition' claim and the new-opt-in AC with the EXISTING `REBAR_MUTATION_ALLOW_UNSANDBOXED` env-var fail-open in `scripts/mutation_sandbox.py:wrap()`: state that a second fail-open branch exists and specify whether the new opt-in supersedes, coexists with, or replaces it.","cohort":["E4"],"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.15,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["scripts/mutation_sandbox.py:268-292 — wrap() has two fail-open branches: `if _ci_environment(env): ... return list(argv)` (270-280) AND `if opt_out_enabled(env): ... return list(argv)` (281-287)","scripts/mutation_sandbox.py:49 `ALLOW_UNSANDBOXED_ENV = \"REBAR_MUTATION_ALLOW_UNSANDBOXED\"`; opt_out_enabled at 194-196 reads it","Plan Summary: 'Ambient `CI` is currently the SOLE condition on that fail-open.'","Plan AC: 'requires an EXPLICIT project opt-in in addition to ambient `CI` — e.g. a config key defaulting to off' — proposes a new opt-in as if none exists"],"finding":"The plan asserts ambient CI is the SOLE condition on the unsandboxed fail-open, but scripts/mutation_sandbox.py:wrap() has a second, independent fail-open branch keyed on the REBAR_MUTATION_ALLOW_UNSANDBOXED env var (opt_out_enabled, lines 281-287). The 'SOLE condition' framing is inaccurate, and — more materially — the AC proposes adding 'an EXPLICIT project opt-in ... e.g. a config key defaulting to off' without ackno